.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-receipt 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-receipt \- Verification receipts: SHA\-keyed claims a named check passed, invalidated by git facts
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten receipt\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Verification receipts: SHA\-keyed claims a named check passed, invalidated by git facts
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
batten\-receipt\-record(1)
Record that the named check concluded pass against the current HEAD
.TP
batten\-receipt\-status(1)
Judge the named check\*(Aqs recorded receipt against HEAD and origin/main
.TP
batten\-receipt\-verified(1)
Is HEAD verified — every declared check\*(Aqs receipt valid against this commit?
.TP
batten\-receipt\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
